WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.620
It’s truly a magnificent feat to have an&nbsp;
ensemble of outstanding characters each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:09.180
with intriguing characteristics and inner&nbsp;
conflicts, to then completely destroy the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:14.040
vast majority of them by the end of the show. And&nbsp;
David and Dan, the showrunners of Game of Thrones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:19.260
somehow managed to do it. So for this video, we&nbsp;
are going to be ranking the top ten characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:23.820
that David and Dan ruined the most and it’s&nbsp;
not like there wasn’t a lot to choose from.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:30.180
Number 10, Euron Greyjoy. Honestly, I really&nbsp;
didn’t know where to place Euron and if I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:34.440
should have even included him on this list to&nbsp;
begin with. Because the thing about show Euron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:39.540
is that he was bad from the get-go. While every&nbsp;
other main character on this list was at one point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:44.580
an outstanding character who you loved dearly.&nbsp;
But Euron on the other hand definitely doesn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:50.040
fit that description. His entrance was laced with&nbsp;
juvenile satire and he wasn’t this menacing and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:54.360
terrifying figure he was supposed to be. Which&nbsp;
is the main reason why I’m including him on this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:59.220
list because his book counterpart is a drastic&nbsp;
upgrade from the show version. I made an entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:03.420
video about this talking about the many issues&nbsp;
of Euron Greyjoy and how to fix his character.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:09.240
The main points were his lack of impact in the&nbsp;
story, his inconsistent goals and motivations, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:14.520
weird cartoonish character direction, and how his&nbsp;
constant usage of annoying comedy was a detriment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:19.740
Show Euron is basically an entirely different&nbsp;
character from his book counterpart and just from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:24.720
that alone I think deserves him a spot on this&nbsp;
list. He may not make you as upset from how bad of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:29.880
a character he is since he was never good, but the&nbsp;
potential was extremely high for him to be great.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:36.420
Number 9, Jaime Lannister. This may seem like&nbsp;
Blasphemy that I’m putting Jaime so low on this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:41.640
ranking, but keep in mind, he was only ruined&nbsp;
during his final episode. Up until that point he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:46.080
genuinely had some good development and I think&nbsp;
his season 7 arc was the best thing about that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:50.520
season. So at least he doesn’t have multiple&nbsp;
seasons worth of development that makes him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:55.980
an atrocious character. And instead just one&nbsp;
episode. Now I used to really hate how Jaime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:59.880
said that he didn’t care for the innocents,&nbsp;
but this could also be interpreted as Jaime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:04.500
using his Kingslayer persona to come across&nbsp;
as being more tough and pushing himself down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:09.240
this hateful path that he’s suddenly on. The&nbsp;
bigger issue to me that still ties into this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:14.100
terrible line is that the writers are taking his&nbsp;
character into a direction that regresses him and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:18.540
undoes his character growth. I think it would&nbsp;
have been perfect to have a mad king mirror in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:22.500
that Cersei was contemplating destroying&nbsp;
the city and Jaime is forced to kill her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:27.960
thus he sacrifices another thing he loves&nbsp;
which is his sister. Losing his honor, skill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:33.360
and love for what is right. Not him suddenly&nbsp;
going back to her despite being appalled by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:38.220
her and dying while trying to flee on a honeymoon&nbsp;
getaway. It makes the Brienne love scene feel like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:43.440
fan service because he abandons her within seconds&nbsp;
after having sex. Surely he should know the fate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:48.240
of Cersei by this point. It fundamentally feels&nbsp;
like a failure to the character’s ending when you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:53.460
can read any other rendition of it and probably&nbsp;
like it significantly more. He’s supposed to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:58.920
this addiction to Cersei, but that was the entire&nbsp;
point of his season 7 arc in that he overcame her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:04.620
toxic grasp and moved on to do good things.&nbsp;
But whatever, I guess the writers disagree.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:10.860
Number 8, Daenerys Targaryen. Like Jaime&nbsp;
Lannister, you’d probably assume that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:16.500
should be further into this list, but she really&nbsp;
wasn’t that bad up until David and Dan decided&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:21.780
to cram an entire mad queen arc in the span of&nbsp;
like two episodes. Or really just one episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:27.360
because before this she was perfectly happy. An&nbsp;
entire arc that should be at minimum an entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:33.000
season long fundamentally doesn’t work in just a&nbsp;
single episode. You lose out on all the detail,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:38.100
slow and believable build-up, and it’s as if David&nbsp;
and Dan are forcing Dany’s character to bend and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:42.540
break into something she’s not. That’s why you&nbsp;
need to take time to slowly progress her to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:48.000
this mad state instead of it literally happening&nbsp;
overnight. She has shown signs of being ruthless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.860
and cold in the past, but her reasoning was always&nbsp;
that these were bad people and she cared about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:57.840
common folk. I can go into a plethora of issues&nbsp;
as to why the whole scenario of her snapping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:03.180
is so devoid of logic, but we already know the&nbsp;
dense layer of dogshit writing that submerges her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:07.800
character here. It completely lacks common sense&nbsp;
and utterly disconnects you from the character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:13.080
because you have no idea why she’s destroying the&nbsp;
entirety of Kingslanding when she already won and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:17.820
should only care about Cersei. So when there’s a&nbsp;
glaringly obvious fix for the writing in having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:23.460
Rhaegal die during the battle of Kingslanding thus&nbsp;
driving Dany to go crazy and act irrationally in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:28.440
the moment, makes me think that David and Dan&nbsp;
had no idea how to execute the mad queen arc.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:32.940
Because as it stands, there was nothing to&nbsp;
drive her over the edge during that moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:37.500
and I don’t know why she was showing so much&nbsp;
restraint up until that point. Such a simple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:42.300
change could have fixed multiple major errors&nbsp;
in the script and it’s just mindboggling to me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:46.920
that they let this happen. Daenerys because of&nbsp;
this has such a contrived ending and when she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:51.240
inevitably dies you barely feel anything&nbsp;
from how compromised her character was.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:58.500
Number 7, Arya Stark. Now Arya Stark as a&nbsp;
character I think is pretty much intact and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:02.760
her overall persona I think is fine within&nbsp;
the later seasons of the show. The primary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:08.220
issue is that David and Dan had no idea how to&nbsp;
utilize her within the story. Because in season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:13.380
7 her entire conflict was about questioning and&nbsp;
challenging her sister which was pretty wild and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:18.480
felt contrived throughout, and then in season&nbsp;
8 she basically had nothing to do. That’s why I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:23.040
primarily believe that David and Dan gave her the&nbsp;
Night King to kill as a consolation prize because,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:28.440
besides that, she doesn’t use any of her faceless&nbsp;
assassin skills. Let alone even using them to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:32.640
kill the Night King. It makes an entire two&nbsp;
season chunk of her journey feel absolutely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:37.200
pointless because she practically has no&nbsp;
payoff for what she went through. That’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:41.820
like watching Rocky train for an entire hour&nbsp;
and then he decides to become a bird watcher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:46.860
in the end. The fact that Jon or anyone don’t&nbsp;
bring up that she can simply assassinate Cersei&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:51.480
with her unique skillset during any meetings&nbsp;
is maddening. It sidelines her character and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:55.320
shifts the spotlight onto Jon and Dany as&nbsp;
they hash out such a jerry-rigged conflict&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.320 --> 00:06:00.540
that makes no sense. Arya’s circumstances is so&nbsp;
heartbreaking from how much of a fan-favorite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:05.100
character she was and how underutilized&nbsp;
she has been since the end of season 6.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:12.180
Number 6, Jon Snow. David and Dan handling&nbsp;
this character is honestly really depressing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:17.340
because he becomes so dull and shallow through&nbsp;
their writing. The second he’s resurrected it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:21.180
feels like he’s just a tool to carry out&nbsp;
the plot and all personality has left the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:26.220
character. Even the internal conflict of being&nbsp;
a Targaryen is so half-baked because David and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:31.320
Dan barely explore it to a good extent, and the&nbsp;
dialogue they write for him is terribly basic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:36.000
and repetitive. So much to the point that it's&nbsp;
become a meme about how much he says muh queen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:41.220
and I don’t want it. But even just developing&nbsp;
the character feels largely skipped over as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:46.140
key scenes like the reveal and him telling his&nbsp;
sisters are extremely rushed. Or just flat out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:51.480
not included. So since the most interesting aspect&nbsp;
of his character is so neutered and downplayed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:56.280
it in turn makes him very uninteresting.&nbsp;
Along with the character literally dying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.280 --> 00:07:00.420
and being brought back to life, but David&nbsp;
and Dan treat that as a get-out-of-jail-free&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:05.760
card instead of a major act that fundamentally&nbsp;
changes him. Forget about how Beric Dondarion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:09.780
says that dying and coming back from the dead&nbsp;
drastically changes you. There’s so much under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:14.400
the surface for Jon Snow to be expanded upon&nbsp;
that it’s just sad that David and Dan don’t go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:19.500
there and rush the story to the point of making&nbsp;
him a generic gooddoer with barely any depth.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:26.640
Number 5, Cersei Lannister. Speaking of characters&nbsp;
that used to be really deep and complex, Cersei&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:31.440
Lannister is basically a husk of what she used&nbsp;
to be in the earlier seasons. Primarily because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:36.720
David and Dan give her nothing to do in the final&nbsp;
seasons. At the absolute bare minimum, she has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:42.000
Jaime in season 7, but once he leaves, season 8&nbsp;
Kingslanding is like a barren wasteland for any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:47.340
developments or characters. We have Bronn who’s&nbsp;
legally not allowed to have scenes with Cersei,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:54.060
Qyburn who basically has no characterization,&nbsp;
a brick wall, and a horny cartoon pirate. Pick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.060 --> 00:08:00.060
your poison! The selection of people for Cersei to&nbsp;
talk to is practically non-existent and it’s very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:04.320
apparent that David and Dan should expand upon&nbsp;
Kingslanding for the sake of Cersei’s character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:09.900
instead of deflating it. Because by stripping&nbsp;
Kingslanding down to nothing, that in turn does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:15.600
the same for Cersei. She has no personal or minor&nbsp;
conflicts to overcome, no one to express herself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:20.460
to, and thus nothing to change and develop&nbsp;
her. Like is she running the entire kingdom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:25.380
by herself? Does she have a new small council?&nbsp;
How is she manipulating the masses into loving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:30.180
her despite killing thousands of them? She’s the&nbsp;
literal queen of Kingslanding which in turn breeds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:36.060
so much conflict and it’s completely unexplored.&nbsp;
Cersei used to be a POV character back in season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:41.040
5 and 6 and it seems like David and Dan stripped&nbsp;
her of that title for the sake of rushing the show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:47.220
to its conclusion. Lena Heady deserved much better&nbsp;
than staring out of windows for most of season 8.

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:52.980
Number 4, Varys. When we're at the point where&nbsp;
the actors playing the characters are clearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:57.840
upset with their direction, then you know&nbsp;
were down bad. Varys was a mysterious and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:02.160
intelligent man who always operated in the&nbsp;
shadows and had a major role in the biggest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:06.840
events of the show. He had great importance&nbsp;
and was a lovable and unique character who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:12.780
had amazing and deeply engaging dialogue scenes&nbsp;
with an equally smart character. After season 4,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:17.760
Varys becomes a punching bag for Tyrion’s&nbsp;
barrage of annoying jokes and basically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:23.160
just becomes a background messenger. Looking&nbsp;
through the entirety of seasons 5,6,7, and 8,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:27.960
the only scene that half resembles him is when&nbsp;
he manipulates that random girl working for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:32.340
Sons of the Harpy for information. Other than&nbsp;
that, he does fuck all and may briefly chime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:37.440
in for some exposition here and there. Gone are&nbsp;
his great discussions with Tyrion, the aura of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:42.840
mystery surrounding his character and what he’s up&nbsp;
to, and any impact he had on the plot. He spends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:48.780
the entirety of season 7 doing nothing and adds&nbsp;
no value to team Daenerys. Like I understand he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:53.160
left behind his little birds in Kingslanding,&nbsp;
but if the man was able to order assassination&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:57.660
attempts on Dany all the way in Essos, then&nbsp;
surely he should know basic information like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:02.520
enemy troop movements. Then for his final outing&nbsp;
they have him suddenly switch his allegiance to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:08.040
Jon despite him being completely devoted to Dany&nbsp;
for almost the entire show. Dany is rightfully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:12.780
upset that she lost her best friend and one&nbsp;
of her children and Varys is immediately like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:18.360
she might be a mad queen everyone abandon ship.&nbsp;
So Varys acts dumb for the sake of scheming and is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:23.880
killed for it. What a waste. Varys is the epitome&nbsp;
of being swept under the rug and being forgotten&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:28.800
about and is another unfortunate casualty of David&nbsp;
and Dan not knowing what to do with a character.

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:35.820
Number 3, Bran Stark. So for Bran, I can buy&nbsp;
the fact that he is a dull husk of a human,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:40.560
but there are two major things that David and Dan&nbsp;
destroy about him. Firstly and most importantly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:45.600
is the fantastical elements surrounding Bran.&nbsp;
This is a character who has proven that he can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:54.060
manipulate the past and essentially travel in&nbsp;
time, and is omniscient. It’s still a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:58.140
confusing to me about how that aspect works&nbsp;
but he does imply at the end of the show that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:02.700
he can see into the future. So the fact that we&nbsp;
have a character that is this busted in terms of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:07.980
strength and is never utilized is outrageous to&nbsp;
me. The whole season 7 conflict with Sansa and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:13.020
Arya should be non-existent because of this and&nbsp;
so should many other conflicts as well. Along&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:17.580
with literally introducing time travel and it&nbsp;
never coming back up again. Bran should of had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:22.080
some major manipulation in terms of the outcome&nbsp;
of the story, but from our perspective he just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:26.520
waits on the sidelines to become king. For all we&nbsp;
know he did manipulate things in the background,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:31.200
but we’ll never know for sure. It seems like that&nbsp;
would be such a cool reveal that Bran is actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:36.120
the most evil person in the show for allowing this&nbsp;
catastrophe to happen, but then this leads into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:41.880
his other glaring issue in that his motivation is&nbsp;
very inconsistent. He has said multiple times that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:46.440
he doesn’t care about anything, and then seemingly&nbsp;
he does care deeply about creating a prosperous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:51.360
realm at his rule. His character just doesn’t make&nbsp;
any sense and I haven’t even gone into the fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:56.400
that David and Dan skipped over an entire season&nbsp;
worth of build-up for his character. Imagine being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.400 --> 00:12:01.680
that lazy that you don’t include a main character&nbsp;
in an entire season of your show, holy shit.

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:07.260
Number 2, Littlefinger. Funnily enough,&nbsp;
Littlefinger has an extremely similar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:11.760
fate as Varys does in terms of how David and&nbsp;
Dan handled his character. What was once one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:15.900
of the smartest and most cunning characters in&nbsp;
the show devolves into a glorified background&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:21.720
character. His intelligent scheming becomes a&nbsp;
confusing and convoluted mess as he simultaneously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:27.000
plays all sides of the coin. He’s doing baffling&nbsp;
things like throwing away Sansa, turning around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:30.960
and making multiple alliances for the sake&nbsp;
of scheming with no real sense of purpose,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:35.880
and then once all of this clearly wasn’t up to&nbsp;
par for the earlier seasons, David and Dan simply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:40.440
stopped trying to do anything with his character.&nbsp;
Even when he comes back into the story in season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:45.360
7, the writers give him such a batshit crazy&nbsp;
objective of getting Sansa to kill Arya that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:50.520
makes you fundamentally question if the character&nbsp;
is OK mentally. Not to mention that it’s massively&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:54.900
contrived as to why Sansa is even trusting&nbsp;
Littlefinger at this point. Littlefinger is like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:58.500
Daenerys in that the writers do something&nbsp;
that utterly compromises the character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:03.900
but for Littlefinger, that happens all the way&nbsp;
back in Season 5 when he betrays Sansa. From&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:07.980
there it’s just never going to be believable about&nbsp;
what he does because the writers don’t understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:13.080
one of his core principles. Then his death is&nbsp;
such an insult to the character that it feels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:18.120
like David and Dan pissed all over his grave. It’s&nbsp;
just a depressing death scene because we witness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:22.920
a character who should be way more intelligent&nbsp;
than this be easily overcome in the most dumb&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:28.500
scheme he ever devised. Him trying to manipulate&nbsp;
Sansa would be like trying to manipulate Ned after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:33.000
betraying him if Joffrey never killed him. It&nbsp;
flat out wouldn’t work and that’s what David&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:38.280
and Dan commit to for his character. So yeah,&nbsp;
rest in peace Littlefinger. I won’t remember&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:43.020
you for your dogshit ending and instead&nbsp;
your legendary chaos is a ladder monologue.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:49.740
Number 1, Tyrion Lannister. There seems to be a&nbsp;
trend that my top 5 most ruined characters all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:54.360
happen to be the most intelligent ones. Maybe&nbsp;
because David and Dan’s intellect wasn’t high&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.360 --> 00:14:00.060
enough to actually write them. But Tyrion to&nbsp;
me was my absolute favorite character and then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:05.160
he quickly becomes my most hated character. He&nbsp;
takes the number 1 spot by such a huge margin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:10.800
that it genuinely makes me very angry. So opening&nbsp;
up the can of worms that is Tyrion post-season 4&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:16.380
is basically an entire video in of itself, but&nbsp;
essentially every single characteristic about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:21.900
him utterly deteriorates. His humor turns into&nbsp;
a juvenile and grating noise that makes my ears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:27.420
bleed, he’s sucked dry of any energy and charisma,&nbsp;
and his intellect does a complete 180 to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:31.800
point that he’s now arguably one of the dumbest&nbsp;
characters. Throughout the entirety of season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:46.320
7 Tyrion purely exists to just nerf Daenerys&nbsp;
and have her not immediately win the war by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:50.820
going straight for Kingslanding. Like the more&nbsp;
you think about it the writers just use Tyrion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:55.020
as a tool to bend the story into the most dumb&nbsp;
directions because he’s deemed as being smart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:59.880
and people listen to him. The biggest example of&nbsp;
this is his plan to capture the wight which ends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:04.500
up being completely pointless and a waste of time&nbsp;
and only exists to give the Night King a dragon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:09.600
Along with him delivering the worst monologue in&nbsp;
the entire show about how great stories make a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:14.280
king. Which makes no sense because he literally&nbsp;
knows what makes a strong and prosperous king.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:19.440
God damn to go from the absolute peak of the show&nbsp;
where he delivers his court monologue imbued with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:25.140
so much hate and passion, to this abysmal piece&nbsp;
of shit gives you mental whiplash. I really need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.140 --> 00:15:28.980
to get around to making a Tyrion Lannister&nbsp;
video because there’s so much to unpack here.

